# What Docker must NOT send to the daemon when building airflow/Dockerfile.
#
# The build context is this whole directory, and everything in it is copied to
# the Docker daemon before the first instruction runs -- so an unfiltered
# context here would ship the local virtualenv and two years of price
# partitions on every build, to install one requirements.txt.
#
# This file has nothing to do with .gitignore. They overlap by coincidence, not
# by design: .gitignore is about what a reader of the repository should see,
# this is about what a build needs. data/ is in both for different reasons.

.venv/
venv/
data/
.git/
.github/
notebooks/
airflow/logs/
airflow/config/
airflow/plugins/
airflow/dags/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.DS_Store
dbt/target/
dbt/logs/
dbt/dbt_packages/
STEP_*_CHECKLIST.md
